--TEST--
a tainted argument at a regex pattern parameter does not compile, and the help names `Core\Regex::quote` with a fix that wraps the argument — `rule:security/launderers-are-sink-named`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:types/qualifiers-tainted-and-secret
// A search word from outside the program is `tainted`.
tainted string $word = "a.b";

// `Core\Regex::compile` takes a pattern, so this line does not compile.
// The error tells you to pass the word through `Core\Regex::quote`.
Core\Regex\Pattern $pattern = Core\Regex::compile($word);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:8:51
%A
  = help: this parameter cannot take `tainted` text. `Core\Regex::quote` makes the text safe for it
  = suggestion (review): pass it through `Core\Regex::quote`: `Core\Regex::quote($word)`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
